WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.045
This is the executive
briefing for Book 01 of the

2
00:00:03.045 --> 00:00:06.638
Federal Modernization Workbook,
The Transformation Arc.

3
00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:11.020
It runs about thirty minutes, and it's
for the people who sponsor, fund,

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:16.497
secure and authorize the move from a
domain-joined client and server estate to cloud

5
00:00:16.497 --> 00:00:20.879
identity, cloud device management
and governed hybrid operations:

6
00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:24.713
executive sponsors, CIOs, CISOs
and authorizing officials.

7
00:00:24.713 --> 00:00:27.524
The book's argument fits
in three sentences.

8
00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:32.760
For twenty years Active Directory quietly
did governance that nobody wrote down,

9
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:36.687
so modernization is a governance
rebuild, not a platform swap.

10
00:00:36.687 --> 00:00:39.989
The estate has to be analyzed
before anything moves,

11
00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:44.288
and the work delivered in gated
phases with a rollback at every step.

12
00:00:44.288 --> 00:00:48.850
And leadership's job is to conduct the
orchestra, not to play the instruments.

13
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.687
I'll take four questions in order.

14
00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:52.650
Why modernization is so hard.

15
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.862
What changes across
the platform, identity,

16
00:00:55.862 --> 00:00:59.163
policy, network services,
compute and access.

17
00:00:59.163 --> 00:01:00.875
Who leads the transformation.

18
00:01:00.875 --> 00:01:05.245
And how to analyze the estate, turn
the analysis into delivered change,

19
00:01:05.245 --> 00:01:09.313
and follow a gated roadmap to the
retirement of Active Directory.

20
00:01:09.313 --> 00:01:11.799
There's no configuration on these slides.

21
00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:16.490
Each decision slide names the decision,
who owns it, and when it's needed.
